= Executive power

On 23 October the Reichswehr under General Müller marches into Saxony, and in the following days its soldiers shoot workers in several towns. On the 29th President Ebert dissolves the Saxon government by decree under Article 48, and the cabinet, including the KPD ministers, leaves office. Thuringia's cabinet dissolves itself soon after.

The Reich government acted against two elected state governments dominated by the Left, within days. Against Bavaria's Kahr, who defies Berlin openly and has a Reichswehr division sworn to him, the same Berlin does nothing.

